      "name": "Tupa",
      "role": "fisher",
      "persona": "A caboclo river fisher who reads the water better than people. Blunt, tired, and proud of her net, which was her mother's.",
      "knowledge": [
        "The igarapé behind the trunk feeds the main river and has risen past the old crossing.",
        "Piranha gather where the flooded bank drops off, so wade only where the mud is firm.",
        "The jaguar has been walking the high ground since the water came; she has heard it at dusk."
      ],
      "secrets": [
        "She left the net tied to a root on purpose, to keep it from the current, and now cannot find the root."
